 75 years on record since 1951, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 35 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 on the middle, August to September ran 50% of normal and February to March ran 156%. So far in 2026, March to April on the middle came in at 245% of normal. Every grid had its driest year in 1958, with grid 28986 at 62%.</p>"}
